        <truefeedback format="html">
          <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p>We know from previous parts that \(a = {@sol1@}\), \(b = {@sol2@}\), \(c = {@sol3@}\) and \(b^2-4ac = {@sol4@}.\) So, using the quadratic formula we get</p>

<p>\(\displaystyle x = \frac{{@-sol2@} \pm \sqrt{{@sol4@}}}{2\times {@sol1@}}\)</p>

<p>\(\displaystyle \quad = \frac{{@-sol2@} \pm {@sqrt(sol4)@}}{2}\)</p>

<p>So \(\displaystyle x = {@sol5@}\) or \(\displaystyle  x = {@sol6@}\).</p>]]></text>
